# JavaScript Function: Zip Two Sequences

```javascript
/**
 * Combines two sequences by producing pairs of elements from corresponding positions.
 * Uses the Array.prototype methods available in modern JavaScript (2023+).
 * 
 * @param {Array} sequence1 - The first input sequence
 * @param {Array} sequence2 - The second input sequence
 * @returns {Array} A new sequence of [element1, element2] pairs
 */
function zip(sequence1, sequence2) {
  return Array.from(
    { length: Math.min(sequence1.length, sequence2.length) },
    (_, index) => [sequence1[index], sequence2[index]]
  );
}

