# JavaScript Function to Cleanse Dataset Column

Here's a self-contained function using **Danfo.js** (a pandas-like library for JavaScript, with recent updates in 2023+):

```javascript
import dfd from "danfo-js-node";

function cleanseColumn(df0, colName) {
  /**
   * Removes all non-alphanumeric characters from a specified column
   * @param {dfd.DataFrame} df0 - The DataFrame to cleanse
   * @param {string} colName - The name of the column to cleanse
   * @returns {dfd.DataFrame} - DataFrame with cleansed column
   */

  // Apply regex replacement to remove non-alphanumeric characters
  const cleanedColumn = df0[colName].apply((val) => {
    if (val === null || val === undefined) return val;
    return String(val).replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9]/g, "");
  });

  // Update the column in the original dataframe
  df0[colName] = cleanedColumn;

  return df0;
}

